<title>CHILE: Chile's Bio Bio sees $271 mln investment.</title>
<headline>Chile's Bio Bio sees $271 mln investment.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean cement producer Cementos Bio Bio SA plans to invest $271 million over the next two years in various projects in its home market, Argentina and Bolivia, CEO Hernan Briones said.</p>
<p>The company, Chile's third largest cement maker, also expects to post 13 billion pesos in profits this year versus 11.6 billion pesos in 1995, Briones told reporters.</p>
<p>The investment projects are in the cement, limestone and forestry sectors, said Briones.</p>
<p>--Rodrigo Martinez, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x214</p>
